---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { footerLinks } from '../data/footerLinks';

const navLinks = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Blog', href: '/blog' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Munglabs">
  <Navbar links={navLinks} />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="pt-28 pb-20 px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <header class="mb-10">
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-mung-600 tracking-wide uppercase">Legal</span>
          <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
            Privacy Policy
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-500">
            Last updated: September 25, 2026
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
          <p>
            Munglabs ("we", "us", or "our") operates the website at
            <a href="https://munglabs.com">https://munglabs.com</a> (the
            "Website"). This Privacy Policy explains what information we
            collect, how we use it, and the choices you have when you use the
            Website.
          </p>

          <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
          <p>We keep our data collection minimal. We only collect:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Your name and email address from your Google Account</strong>,
              when you sign in using Sign in with Google (Google OAuth). We
              only request your name and email — we do not request access to your
              Gmail, Drive, Contacts, or any other Google data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Account data you submit to us</strong> when you create an
              account or contact us (for example, by emailing
              <a href="mailto:contact@munglabs.com">contact@munglabs.com</a>).
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            When you sign in with Google, Google provides us with your name and
            email address. We associate that email address with your account on
            our services. We do not link the same email to multiple identities
            and we do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with
            third parties for marketing purposes.
          </p>

          <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>To identify you and create and maintain your account.</li>
            <li>To provide and improve our services, including personalized features.</li>
            <li>To respond to your questions and support requests.</li>
            <li>To detect abuse, prevent fraud, and keep the service secure.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>3. Legal basis</h2>
          <p>
            We process your personal information where we have your consent (when
            you sign in), where it is necessary to perform the service you
            requested, or where we have a legitimate interest in operating and
            securing our services.
          </p>

          <h2>4. How we share information</h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell your personal information. We may share your name and
            email with:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Google</strong>, solely to the extent required to verify
              your Google sign-in (Google receives your name and email as the
              account holder; we do not send them elsewhere).
            </li>
            <li>Service providers who help us operate the service (for example,
              hosting), under contractual obligations to protect your data.</li>
            <li>Authorities, where required by law or to protect our rights.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>5. Third-party services on this site</h2>
          <p>
            This Website uses the following third-party technologies, each of
            which may collect information as described in their own privacy
            policies:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Google Sign-In (OAuth)</strong> — handles your sign-in at
              Google. Google may collect information about your interaction with
              the sign-in flow. See Google's
              <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Giscus</strong> (comments on blog posts) — comment threads
              are stored on and served from GitHub. Giscus uses a GitHub account
              to authenticate commenters and sets cookies for that purpose. See
              Giscus'
              <a href="https://giscus.app/privacy-policy.html">Privacy Policy</a>
              and
              <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service">GitHub's Terms</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Google Fonts</strong> — web fonts are served by Google.
              Browsers may share your IP address and user agent with Google when
              loading fonts.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not run web analytics (such as Google Analytics) on this Website.</p>

          <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            We use strictly necessary session cookies to keep you signed in.
            Third parties (Giscus, Google) may set their own cookies as
            described above. You can control cookies through your browser
            settings.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            We keep your account information (name and email) for as long as
            your account is active. You can request deletion of your account and
            associated data at any time by contacting us.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access,
            correct, export, or delete your personal data, and to object to or
            restrict its processing. To exercise any of these rights, email us
            at <a href="mailto:contact@munglabs.com">contact@munglabs.com</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our services are not directed to children under 13 (or the
            equivalent minimum age in your jurisdiction), and we do not
            knowingly collect personal information from them.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Security</h2>
          <p>
            We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect
            your personal information, including encryption in transit (HTTPS).
          </p>

          <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The Last
            updated date at the top of this page reflects the most recent
            revision. Material changes will be posted on this page.
          </p>

          <h2>12. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:contact@munglabs.com">contact@munglabs.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer links={footerLinks} />
</BaseLayout>
